    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ga2o4ba",
      "content": "Uttarakhand's history spans thousands of years, with evidence of habitation dating to the Vedic period. The region finds mention in ancient texts as 'Kedarkhand' (present Garhwal) and 'Manaskhand' (present Kumaon). The Mahabharata and Puranas describe it as the abode of gods and sages."
    },
    {
      "id": "f51gjeg",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "g4xsy2a",
      "src": "/books/Guide/Uttarakhand_CONSTABLE/images/image_g4xsy2a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "onwjrrc",
      "content": "The Khasas were the earliest identifiable people of the hills. The region was home to the Kuninda Kingdom (around 2nd century BCE–2nd century CE), whose coins have been found near Almora and Srinagar (Garhwal). The Kuninda ruler Amoghbhuti is mentioned in inscriptions."
    },
