    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ow05xbu",
      "content": "Vir Chandra Singh Garhwali is particularly celebrated — a soldier of the Royal Garhwal Rifles who refused orders to fire on unarmed Pathans in Peshawar during the Civil Disobedience Movement (1930). He was sentenced to life imprisonment. His birth anniversary (25 December) is celebrated as 'Vir Garhwali Diwas'."
    },
    {
      "id": "rn8x09v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.5 Formation of Uttarakhand State"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Katyuri Dynasty is recognized as the first historical royal dynasty that ruled a major part of Uttarakhand.",
        "Treaty of Sugauli (1815) established the Kali River as the eastern international border of Uttarakhand.",
        "The state was initially created as 'Uttaranchal' in 2000 and officially renamed 'Uttarakhand' on January 1, 2007."
      ],
      "id": "yo0u02h"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zvgrvqa",
      "content": "The demand for a separate hill state began seriously in the 1950s. The main arguments were neglect of hill districts in development, lack of employment, and cultural distinct identity. The movement intensified after 1994."
    },
